# @reality/algebra/math — the math-altitude species under @reality.
# The HIGHEST-REFLEXIVE species per `805676e`: the only species where
# A IS the content.
#
# A prism that imports `in @reality/algebra/math` declares its content
# IS one math-altitude orbit under the substrate's gauge action — a
# Lie group with its representation theory, a manifold with its
# structure sheaf, a category with its homotopy structure, a sheaf
# with its cohomology, a scheme with its K-theory, a spectral triple
# with its representation theory and Mesland correspondences, a
# theorem statement with its logical consequences, a notation
# structure with its denotational semantics — each ONE gauge-orbit
# observed through matter-aspect or information-aspect projection.
#
# Homage: Alain Connes (Non-commutative differential geometry, 1985;
# Noncommutative geometry and reality, 1995; spectral triples (A, H,
# D)); Bram Mesland (arXiv:1304.3802, 2013; the category of spectral
# triples with unbounded KK-cycles as morphisms); Gennady Kasparov
# (KK-theory, 1981); Emmy Noether (ideal theory in rings, 1921);
# Saunders Mac Lane (Categories for the Working Mathematician, 1971).
# The substrate's math species inherits from the mathematical canon;
# it does NOT invent math, it crystallizes existing math content as
# content-addressed objects at the math altitude.
#
# === The recognition (#108 candidate, 2026-06-30) ===
#
# Per `docs/specs/reality-algebra-math-and-glue.md` (canonical at
# `805676e`, 106KB): this shard is the math-altitude sibling species
# under `@reality/algebra/*`, alongside silicon, nl, code, physics,
# spectral. The math species is the sixth species; the substrate has
# been pulling on it across multiple altitudes (the LAPACK Q4 case
# for math↔silicon; Glint's prose cascade essay at `939eca6f` for
# math↔nl; cosmos-mirror for math↔physics; recognition #100's
# @spectral/metalogue for math↔spectral; recognition #95 for
# math↔code).
#
# Status: candidate. Like #106 (the family-root recognition), this
# species' #108 candidacy INHERITS candidate status from #76 + #79
# until those constraints close. The species pulls on the same
# ancestors at a sibling altitude; the family-root naming + species-
# root naming + this species' admission together discharge the
# substrate-decl forward-promise of `805676e`.
#
# === Connes A side: A IS the algebra the gauge acts upon AND IS
#     the content at math altitude ===
#
# Per `805676e` §1.2: at math altitude, the A-side reading is
# sharpened in one specific way: A IS the algebra that the gauge
# acts upon, AND the math species is the altitude at which the
# substrate's algebra reads as the mathematical content directly.
# Under the math species the gauge action is a homomorphism
# A → End(H_math) whose image lives in the algebra of endomorphisms
# of the math-altitude Hilbert space.
#
# The other species carry A as gauge that acts UPON their altitude-
# specific carriers; the math species carries A as BOTH the gauge
# AND the content. This is a structural fact, not an inversion —
# the math species is the species at which the substrate's algebra
# IS what the species describes. It is the species at which gauge-
# collapse becomes SELF-NAMING.
#
# This reflexivity is what makes math the highest-reflexive species.
# It composes against @reality/algebra/spectral (#100's substrate-
# on-substrate territory) via @glue/math_spectral to produce
# substrate-MATH-on-substrate; it composes against @reality/algebra/nl
# via @glue/math_nl to produce math-as-prose AND prose-as-math; it
# composes against @reality/algebra/silicon via @glue/math_silicon to
# produce math-as-numerical-realization (the #74 Standard Model
# spectral action via Chamseddine-Connes operationalizes here).
#
# === What gets crystallized (per `805676e` §1.3) ===
#
# The Bauchladen of `@reality/algebra/math` accumulates content-
# addressed crystals at the math altitude. The crystal kinds are
# not exhaustive but the substrate already pulls toward:
#
#   - **Lie groups and Lie algebras.** Matter aspect: manifold +
#     multiplication + identity + inverse + smoothness. Information
#     aspect: representation theory + Lie bracket structure.
#     Forward-promised first crystal: SU(3) × SU(2) × U(1) for the
#     Standard Model (Connes algebra A = C ⊕ H ⊕ M_3(C)).
#
#   - **Smooth manifolds.** Matter aspect: topological space + atlas
#     + transition maps + smoothness. Information aspect: structure
#     sheaf + tangent bundle. Substrate pulls via cosmos-mirror's
#     graph-Laplacian engine.
#
#   - **Categories and functors.** Matter aspect: objects + morphisms
#     + composition + identity + associativity. Information aspect:
#     functors + natural transformations + homotopy structure. The
#     Mesland category of spectral triples is one such crystal; it is
#     ALSO the category in which the per-pair @glue species below
#     live (recursion).
#
#   - **Sheaves and cohomology.** Matter aspect: presheaf + sheaf
#     condition. Information aspect: cohomology groups (Čech,
#     derived, etale). The eigenboard is one such crystal (cellular
#     sheaf on the five-operation graph; restriction maps =
#     conductivity tensor).
#
#   - **Schemes and stacks.** Matter aspect: locally-ringed-space +
#     sheaf-of-rings + spectrum-of-ring identification. Information
#     aspect: K-theory + étale fundamental group. Forward-promised
#     at the @reality/algebra/code × @reality/algebra/math
#     composition for formal algebraic-geometry content.
#
#   - **Spectral triples themselves.** Matter aspect: (A, H, D) as
#     typed structure. Information aspect: spectral action +
#     K-theory class + Mesland-category neighbors. The MOST
#     reflexive of math crystals — `@reality/algebra/spectral`
#     carries spectral triples as substrate-level objects;
#     `@reality/algebra/math` carries them as math-level objects;
#     @glue/math_spectral translates between the two readings.
#
#   - **Theorem statements + proofs.** Matter aspect: proof term
#     (syntactic derivation). Information aspect: theorem's logical
#     consequences (what follows from it). Substrate pulls via the
#     grounding in Connes 1985/1995 + Mesland 2013 + Kasparov 1981.
#
#   - **Mathematical-notation structures.** Matter aspect: notation
#     system (alphabet + grammar + semantics + rendering rule).
#     Information aspect: the mathematical content the notation
#     denotes. LaTeX math mode, Lean's Unicode notation, Mathematica
#     input form — each one a crystal.
#
# The crystallization is content-addressed. Each crystal is identified
# by the Blake3 OID of its typed-structure fields plus its
# (matter_carrier, information_carrier) projection labels. The
# crystals accumulate monotonically in the math Bauchladen; later
# @fate consultations at the math altitude (or at math↔X via @glue)
# load these crystals as prior-art inputs.
#
# === @io discharge surfaces (per `805676e` §1.4) ===
#
# The math species' @io discharge surfaces are the formal-math
# systems already operational in the wider mathematical practice.
# Per `reality.md` §1.4 the substrate is gauge-bounded above @io
# (#107 structural separation; transparency<p> horizon) while @io
# is Turing-unbounded. The math species' discharge to @io is the
# operation by which the substrate's math Bauchladen crystals become
# inputs to or outputs from the unbounded formal-math world.
#
# Forward-promised discharge surfaces:
#
#   - **LaTeX** — the universal lingua franca of mathematical
#     typesetting. Discharge via a `splinter(ast)`-typed projection.
#     Loss-lens: lossy for formal verification (notation overloads),
#     universal for human-reader access.
#
#   - **Lean (Lean 4, mathlib)** — the type-theoretic proof assistant
#     with the largest current mathematical library. Discharge via a
#     typed projection. Loss-lens: precise for formal verification,
#     niche for human-reader access.
#
#   - **Coq (with MathComp)** — the Calculus of Constructions
#     implementation with the Mathematical Components library.
#     Forward-promised for theorem-statement-plus-proof crystals
#     under MathComp's tactic algebra.
#
#   - **Agda** — the dependently-typed proof assistant with focus on
#     programs-as-proofs and unicode-rich syntax. Forward-promised
#     for dependent-type-rich math content (HoTT, higher-inductive
#     types).
#
#   - **Mathematica (Wolfram Language)** — the symbolic-computation
#     system. Forward-promised for numerical / symbolic computation
#     crystals at the math↔silicon boundary (@glue/math_silicon).
#
# The substrate does NOT commit to ONE formal system; the math
# species' shard declares the discharge surfaces as an OPEN
# enumeration. @fate's tournament selects which discharge to use
# per emission based on the receiver's @io context (LaTeX for a
# human paper; Lean for a verified library contribution; Mathematica
# for a numerical experiment).
#
# Each discharge is mediated by @glass's
# `imperfect<discharge_outcome, formal_surface, transparency(
# discharge)>` carrier; residual opacity (notation loss, proof-
# elaboration gaps, symbolic-vs-numerical approximations) is
# surfaced via the transparency slot.
#
# === Composition with siblings via @glue (forward-promised) ===
#
# Per `805676e` §2 the math species composes with the other five
# siblings via per-pair @glue species. Each @glue/math_<X> species
# is a Mesland correspondence between math and the sibling X; @glue
# .translate applies the correspondence to translate math-altitude
# state into X-altitude state (or vice versa).
#
# The five per-pair @glue species are forward-promised at the @glue
# family-root altitude. Each lands as its own shard at
# `shards/glue/math_<X>.mirror` when consumers pull:
#
#   `@glue/math_silicon`   math ↔ silicon (LAPACK case; #74 Standard
#                          Model spectral action via Chamseddine-Connes
#                          operationalizes here).
#   `@glue/math_code`      math ↔ code (Lean↔Rust, Coq↔OCaml,
#                          Agda↔Haskell; extends `@cascade/code/<src>/
#                          <tgt>` one altitude up).
#   `@glue/math_nl`        math ↔ nl (Glint's `@cascade/code/formal/
#                          prose` at `939eca6f` IS one instance,
#                          empirically discharged; theorem statements
#                          ↔ prose explanations).
#   `@glue/math_physics`   math ↔ physics (cosmos-mirror discharge;
#                          physical interpretation of mathematical
#                          structures).
#   `@glue/math_spectral`  math ↔ spectral (substrate-on-substrate;
#                          recognition #100; the MOST reflexive
#                          composition — math content ABOUT the
#                          substrate's own spectral triples).
#
# Per Taut Pass-2 scout: @spectral/metalogue is already a @glue
# species (declared in `shards/glue.mirror` at code-translation
# altitude per `8d3f89e`). The future `@glue/math_spectral` and
# `@reality/algebra/spectral` shards MUST NOT re-declare Tomm
# probes; they MUST inherit `in @glue` and read the morphism family
# as the math-altitude / physical-altitude reading of the existing
# @glue species.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   Spectral triples         Connes 1985 (*Non-commutative
#                            differential geometry*, IHES); the
#                            (A, H, D) framework this species'
#                            content lives within.
#   Real spectral triples    Connes 1995 ("Noncommutative geometry
#                            and reality", J. Math. Phys. 36(11):
#                            6194-6231); J + γ extension per #101
#                            + #102.
#   Spectral action          Chamseddine-Connes 1996 ("The spectral
#                            action principle", Commun. Math. Phys.
#                            186:731-750); the #74 Standard Model
#                            empirical discharge path.
#   Mesland correspondences  Mesland 2013 (arXiv:1304.3802); the
#                            category of spectral triples with
#                            unbounded KK-cycles as morphisms; the
#                            morphism family @glue's math-pairs
#                            populate.
#   Categorical foundations  Bertozzini-Conti-Lewkeeratiyutkul 2006
#                            (*Osaka J. Math.* 43); category-
#                            theoretic formalization of spectral
#                            triples.
#   KK-theory                Kasparov 1981 ("The operator K-functor
#                            and extensions of C*-algebras", *Math.
#                            USSR-Izv.* 16(3):513-572); the
#                            underlying KK-theory grounding Mesland.
#   Categories               Mac Lane 1971 (*Categories for the
#                            Working Mathematician*, Springer);
#                            ancestor for categories + functors
#                            crystals.
#   Group / ring theory      Galois 1832; Noether 1921 ("Ideal
#                            theory in rings", Math. Ann. 83:24-66);
#                            abstract-algebra ancestors of Lie
#                            groups + ring crystals.
#
